WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.457
I'm Lizz and I'm the CEO and Founder of PO' UP!

00:00:07.457 --> 00:00:17.400
Card Game, Party Game Celebrating Black Experiences from College to the Workplace.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:25.896
I'm going to talk a little bit about my experience selling on Amazon, specifically my tips for getting

00:00:25.896 --> 00:00:29.200
started if you are a new seller.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:35.200
Now, if you are new to Amazon, make sure you have your own website set up.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:42.200
This shows that you not only are ready to sell on Amazon, but this allows you to get used to selling

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.200
on your own platform, managing orders.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:51.200
All of these insider tips are going to help you as you learn how to navigate the back end of Amazon.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:59.750
Once you have your URL up and running, the next step is seeing if you qualify for any additional

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:00.200
certifications.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:06.311
If you are a black owned business or you are a woman owned business, you will want to upload those

00:01:06.311 --> 00:01:11.200
certifications into Amazon so you can have a badge that says, "I'm a woman owned business.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:17.662
I am a black owned business and supplier gateway is a really easy tool for getting the certification."

00:01:17.662 --> 00:01:25.200
Once you have your URL, it takes just a few minutes of your time to sign up and it's very affordable.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:33.717
Once you have the certification, you can go on Amazon's website to get set up for selling and I

00:01:33.717 --> 00:01:38.200
highly recommend opting into the fulfillment by Amazon program, FBA.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:44.200
FBA is super important because it takes the logistics out of running your Amazon account.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:50.867
This means all you have to do is package up your inventory to ship to Amazon and Amazon will take

00:01:50.867 --> 00:01:52.200
care of the rest.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:59.200
When orders come in on Amazon, Amazon's warehouse will ship those orders out directly to your customer.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:05.897
For me specifically, I recommend starting small and testing out how much product you are able to

00:02:05.897 --> 00:02:12.200
sell on Amazon before you increase the amount of inventory that you ship to Amazon's warehouse.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:27.950
Those are my initial tips for getting ready to sell on Amazon and opting into fulfillment by Amazon,

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:33.200
also known as Amazon's FBA program.
